{"name":"Red Pear","hex":"#82383c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"pear","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible fruit produced by the pear tree, similar to an apple but typically elongated towards the stem.","A type of fruit tree (Pyrus communis)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pear"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pyrus communis","blocks":[{"text":"Pyrus communis, the common pear, is a species of pear native to central and eastern Europe, and western Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Pears.jpg/330px-Pears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pyrus_communis"},{"title":"Pear","blocks":[{"text":"Pears are a genus of trees, Pyrus, in the family Rosaceae, that bear an edible apple-like fruit of the same name. Several species of pears are cultivated for their fruit and juices, while others are grown as ornamental flowering trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Pears.jpg/330px-Pears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pear"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"},{"title":"Shades of yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color yellow may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a yellow or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Color_icon_yellow.svg/330px-Color_icon_yellow.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg/250px-2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg/330px-2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg/250px-2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2015_Kwiatostan_gruszy_pospolitej.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Kru%C5%A1ka_Rana_Moretini_-_mali_plodov